---
/**
 * Groups the Mentor Game Studio era's entries (Mitko's solo-era mentor work
 * through the reunion) so they stay one unit for the tag-filter cascade —
 * purely structural, no visible styling of its own. The era's actual "box"
 * identity comes from its contents: Mitko's under-mentor track gets its own
 * enclosing envelope confined to his column (see ApartBlock.astro's
 * `.track.under-mentor`, headed by the "Mentor Game Studio" / date label),
 * and the reunion (Together Again) is a full-width `company.emphasized` box
 * wrapped in the warm mentor envelope (see CompanyBlock.astro) once both of
 * them are back together — Ádám's side stays plain background for
 * everything in between, since he isn't part of Mentor Game Studio until
 * that point. In reversed direction the "MENTOR GAME STUDIO" label rides
 * inside Together Again's envelope instead of Mitko's (see
 * CompanyBlock.astro's `.mentor-envelope-heading`), so this container has
 * no label of its own to render — the labels live in the era's endpoints.
 */
---

<div class="mentor-container">
	<div class="mentor-content">
		<slot />
	</div>
</div>

<style>
	.mentor-container {
		width: 100%;
	}

	.mentor-content {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 2rem;
	}

	/* Hidden by default; the reversed-timeline CSS in Timeline.astro flips this
	   on so the "MENTOR GAME STUDIO" label stays at the visual top of the era
	   even when Together Again is the entry now sitting there. Mirrors the
	   `.mentor-heading` markup inside ApartBlock (see there for the base look). */
	.mentor-era-heading {
		display: none;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.1rem;
		padding: 0 1.5rem 0.75rem;
	}

	.mentor-era-name {
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.16em;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--mentor);
		text-shadow: 0 0 14px var(--mentor-soft);
	}

	.mentor-era-dates {
		font-size: 0.72rem;
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
		letter-spacing: 0.05em;
		color: var(--fg-muted);
	}
</style>
